; shapes.eval - EditorTest phase 17 (tool-refinement Phase 6): the shape
; brushes - corridor, room, stamp, region - laid in the current style.
;
; Run on a FIXTURE the test writes into eval_arena first (and puts back after):
; solid rock, 28x24, but for a 5x5 room round the start at 14,12 - so every
; brush has rock to open. Small Crypt is the style: crypt_passage for a
; corridor, crypt_chamber for a room.
logecho on
reset
timescale 0
freeze on

echo --- base ---
mapinfo
geomhash
style use small_crypt
editor shape seed 7

; --- a corridor out of the room, undone and redone --------------------------------
echo --- corridor ---
editor shape corridor 12 12 3 3
mapinfo
undo
mapinfo
; An undo defers reloading the surfaces until the editor closes (the theme's
; wall type the corridor enrolled has to come off the palette), so close it
; and let a frame run before measuring.
editor off
step 0.1
geomhash
redo
mapinfo

; --- a room on its own, a stamp over the start room, a region below it ---------
echo --- room ---
editor shape room 18 3 24 8
echo --- stamp ---
editor shape stamp pillared_hall 14 12 0
echo --- region ---
editor shape region 12 15 22 22

; --- no style: plain carving; a region too small to generate in -----------------
echo --- plain ---
style use off
editor shape room 24 12 26 14
editor shape region 2 18 5 21
savemap
